<figure id="Sx4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Ablation experiments of PromptTea modules. The values in parentheses represent the threshold of the method. PromptTea is defined as TeaCache+ <math id="Sx4.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>+<math id="Sx4.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>+PCA. The numbers inside the parentheses of PromptTea(0.1, 0.23) represent that the upper and lower threshold limits <math id="Sx4.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx4.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <span id="Sx4.T2.2" class="ltx_text">Eq. <a href="#Sx3.E7" title="In Prompt Complexity Aware ‣ PromptTea ‣ Methodology ‣ PromptTea: Let Prompts Tell TeaCache the Optimal Threshold" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></span> are 0.1 and 0.23 respectively.</figcaption>
<table id="Sx4.T2.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
