</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Comparison of correlations among timpstep embedding, TEMNI, and output. </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx6.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Sx6.F10.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06739v1/img/cog-fit.png" id="Sx6.F10.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/419;" width="698" height="419" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>CogVideoX1.5</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Sx6.F10.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06739v1/img/hun-fit.png" id="Sx6.F10.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/419;" width="698" height="419" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>HunyuanVideo</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Sx6.F10.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06739v1/img/wan-fit.png" id="Sx6.F10.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/419;" width="698" height="419" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Wan2.1</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Input-output relationship fitting results: The green curves denote our polynomial fitting, the red curves represent TeaCache’s model, and black dots indicate ground-truth label values. Comparative analysis shows that our fitting demonstrates significantly higher accuracy in capturing the input-output dynamics than TeaCache.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Table shows the mean squared error (MSE) values, with units of <math id="Sx6.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, obtained by comparing the output curves of Teacache and PromptTea algorithms against a set of labels. It is evident that PromptTea has smaller MSE values, indicating a more precise fit.</figcaption>
